# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# QS-VC Environment Configuration
# Copy to .env and fill in values
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# General
NODE_ENV=development

# SFU Service
SFU_PORT=4000
SFU_ANNOUNCED_IP=127.0.0.1
SFU_MIN_PORT=40000
SFU_MAX_PORT=49999
SFU_NUM_WORKERS=2
SFU_LOG_LEVEL=debug

# Signaling Service
SIGNALING_PORT=4001
SIGNALING_SFU_URL=http://localhost:4000

# Auth Service
AUTH_PORT=4002
JWT_SECRET=dev-jwt-secret-change-in-production
JWT_EXPIRY=24h

# Meeting Service
MEETING_PORT=4003
WEB_URL=http://localhost:5173

# Recording Service
RECORDING_PORT=4004

# Web Client
VITE_SIGNALING_URL=ws://localhost:4001/ws
VITE_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:4002
VITE_MEETING_URL=http://localhost:4003
VITE_RECORDING_URL=http://localhost:4004
VITE_APP_NAME=QS-VC

# PostgreSQL
POSTGRES_HOST=localhost
POSTGRES_PORT=5432
POSTGRES_DB=qsvc
POSTGRES_USER=qsvc
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=qsvc_dev_2025

# Redis
REDIS_HOST=localhost
REDIS_PORT=6379

# MinIO (S3-compatible)
MINIO_ENDPOINT=localhost
MINIO_PORT=9000
MINIO_ACCESS_KEY=qsvc_minio
MINIO_SECRET_KEY=qsvc_minio_secret
MINIO_BUCKET=qsvc-recordings

# TURN/STUN
TURN_SECRET=dev-turn-secret-change-in-production
TURN_SERVERS=turn:localhost:3478

# Official Google Cloud Translation (server only; prepared adapter, not yet exposed)
# Enable Translation API/billing and restrict this key. Never prefix it with VITE_.
GOOGLE_TRANSLATE_API_KEY=

# Existing meeting translation connector (trusted server base URL; optional)
LIBRETRANSLATE_URL=
LIBRETRANSLATE_API_KEY=

# Cloud RDS: verify-full plus the AWS RDS CA bundle file.
# Intranet: point POSTGRES_HOST at the organisation's local database.
# POSTGRES_SSL=verify-full
# POSTGRES_CA_FILE=/absolute/path/to/ap-south-1-bundle.pem
# DB_APPLICATION_NAME=qsvc-cloud

# Separate restricted login URLs for hosted services (set privately, never VITE_).
# AUTH_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://qs_auth_app:ENCODED_PASSWORD@RDS_ENDPOINT:5432/qsvc
# MEETING_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://qs_meeting_app:ENCODED_PASSWORD@RDS_ENDPOINT:5432/qsvc

# Platform admins (full access to every feature). Comma-separated; defaults to the built-in list when unset.
QSVC_ADMIN_EMAILS=services@madylabs.xyz,contact@neurqai.com,smrita.official@gmail.com
# Admin online test workspace; this is shared qsvcmeet.com, not isolated intranet hosting.
QSVC_ADMIN_WORKSPACE_URL=https://qsvcmeet.com
# Local auth development only; production AWS uses the read-only compose mount.
# ENTERPRISE_WINDOWS_INSTALLER=/absolute/path/to/QS-VC-Windows-x64.zip
# ENTERPRISE_MACOS_ARM64_INSTALLER=/absolute/path/to/QS-VC-macOS-arm64.zip
# ENTERPRISE_MACOS_X64_INSTALLER=/absolute/path/to/QS-VC-macOS-x64.zip
# Leave unset. Set to yes only while the platform admins create their accounts, then remove it.
# QSVC_ADMIN_SIGNUP_OPEN=yes

# Production SFU control. Use the same random secret in SFU and signaling.
# SFU_CONTROL_TOKEN=

# Optional enterprise MCU path (FreeSWITCH + drachtio; see deploy/poly-bridge).
# The intranet launcher accepts MCU_ENABLED=true (legacy) or
# POLY_BRIDGE_ENABLED=true and fails fast unless these dependencies are reachable.
# POLY_BRIDGE_ENABLED=false
# MCU_ENABLED=false
# BRIDGE_API_TOKEN=
# FS_ESL_HOST=10.0.0.20
# FS_ESL_PORT=8021
# FS_ESL_PASSWORD=
# DRACHTIO_HOST=10.0.0.20
# DRACHTIO_PORT=9022
# DRACHTIO_SECRET=
# BRIDGE_RTP_ANNOUNCED_IP=<SFU address reachable from FreeSWITCH>

# Enable in both auth and signaling for a private workspace with provisioned accounts.
# QSVC_ENTERPRISE_TERMS_REQUIRED=yes
